PART 3: EXTRACTING AND STORING THE IMAGE URL

================================================================================

Step 1: Update State with Image URL

The API provides the image URL through:

data.message


Store this value in React state.

import React, { useState } from 'react';

export default function App() {

  const [imageUrl, setImageUrl] = useState('');

  const getRandomDog = async () => {

    const response = await fetch(
      'https://dog.ceo/api/breeds/image/random'
    );

    const data = await response.json();

    // Extract image URL from API response
    const dogImageUrl = data.message;

    // Store it in state
    setImageUrl(dogImageUrl);
  };

  return (
    <div>

      <h2>Random Puppy</h2>

      <button onClick={getRandomDog}>
        Get Random Puppy
      </button>

    </div>
  );
}

Code Explanation
Code                             | Explanation
---------------------------------|----------------------------------------------
data.message                     | Contains the image URL returned by API
const dogImageUrl = data.message | Extracts URL into a separate variable
setImageUrl(dogImageUrl)         | Stores the URL in imageUrl state


When setImageUrl() updates the state:

API Response
     ↓
data.message
     ↓
dogImageUrl
     ↓
setImageUrl(dogImageUrl)
     ↓
imageUrl State Updated
     ↓
Component Re-renders


