PART 4: DYNAMICALLY DISPLAYING THE IMAGE

================================================================================

Step 1: Add Image Tag with Dynamic Source

Use the URL stored in imageUrl as the image source.

import React, { useState } from 'react';

export default function App() {

  const [imageUrl, setImageUrl] = useState('');

  const getRandomDog = async () => {

    const response = await fetch(
      'https://dog.ceo/api/breeds/image/random'
    );

    const data = await response.json();

    setImageUrl(data.message);
  };

  return (
    <div>

      <h2>Random Puppy</h2>

      <button onClick={getRandomDog}>
        Get Random Puppy
      </button>

      {imageUrl && (
        <img
          src={imageUrl}
          alt="Random Puppy"
        />
      )}

    </div>
  );
}

Code Explanation
Code                     | Explanation
-------------------------|---------------------------------------------
imageUrl &&              | Render only when imageUrl contains a value
<img ... />              | Displays the dog image
src={imageUrl}           | Gets image source dynamically from state
alt="Random Puppy"       | Provides alternative/accessibility text

Conditional Rendering
{imageUrl && <img src={imageUrl} alt="Random Puppy" />}


How it works:

imageUrl is empty
       ↓
Condition is false
       ↓
Nothing is displayed


imageUrl contains URL
       ↓
Condition is true
       ↓
Image is displayed

Dynamic Source
src={imageUrl}


Flow:

API
 ↓
data.message
 ↓
setImageUrl()
 ↓
imageUrl State
 ↓
src={imageUrl}
 ↓
Image Displayed


When imageUrl changes, React automatically re-renders the component with the new image.

